.TH TRAJECTORY 2
.SH NAME
Trajectory \- interface and live client for planar flight models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "danby/trajectory.m";
modelmodule: Trajectory;

modelmodule = load Trajectory path;
model := modelmodule->new();
state := modelmodule->initialstate(model);
modelmodule->evaluate(model,t,state,derivative);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Trajectory
separates signed planar equations of motion from integration and display.
Implementations provide mutable parameters, labels and display ranges, a fresh
initial [x,y,vx,vy] state, and a right-hand-side evaluation function.
.PP
.B /dis/temple/trajectory.dis
is the reusable live client.  It advances the state with
.IR numerics (2),
stores named Plot data, draws physical height against distance and speed against
time, and detects the first descending ground crossing by interpolation.
Unlike
.IR populationmodel (2),
it does not clamp signed velocity components.
.SH FILES
.B /module/danby/trajectory.m
.br
.B /appl/temple/trajectory.b
.br
.B /dis/temple/trajectory.dis
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR plot (2),
.IR numerics (2),
.IR populationmodel (2)
